 {
  "id": "wa_klawatti_peak_north_ridge",
  "name": "North Ridge",
  "discipline": "mountaineering",
  "grade": "Class 4",
  "verdict": "SUMMIT_ONLY",
  "state": "wa",
  "peak": {
   "id": "wa_klawatti_peak",
   "name": "Klawatti Peak",
   "lat": 48.5544,
   "lng": -121.1044,
   "elevation_ft": 8485,
   "region": "Washington",
   "path": "usa.washington.wa_northwest.wa_hwy20_ncnp.wa_north_cascades.wa_north_cascades_core.wa_klawatti_peak"
  },
  "text": {
   "approach": "From Marblemount on WA-20, drive the Cascade River Road (FR-15) about 19-21 miles (paved to roughly mile 10, then gravel/washboard) to the Eldorado trailhead (~2,150 ft). Cross the North Fork Cascade River and follow the unmaintained Eldorado climbers' trail through forest and a boulder field to treeline, then to Eldorado Basin/Roush Creek camps (~6,000-6,300 ft). Ascend the Eldorado Glacier snow dome to the ~7,500-ft notch on Eldorado's lower East Ridge, traverse ~1.5 miles north across the upper Inspiration Glacier to Klawatti Col (7,800 ft), then continue easily to the nearby Klawatti-Austera Col (7,900 ft) to start the ridge.",
   "approach_logistics": null,
   "road": "{\"name\":\"Cascade River Road (FR-15)\",\"status\":\"Open (paved to ~mile 10, gravel/washboard beyond)\",\"driveNote\":\"Narrow gravel road; no RVs or trailers over 22 ft; Eldorado trailhead near road mile 20-21\",\"seasonalGate\":\"Typically snow-gated in winter; sometimes washes out and requires Forest Service repair\"}",
   "overview": "A Class 3 scramble along Klawatti's north ridge from the Klawatti-Austera Col, working around a rock tower nicknamed 'The Smokestack' before finishing on the summit crest.",
   "description": null,
