   "region": "Washington",
   "path": "usa.washington.wa_centraleast.wa_stuart_range.wa_little_annapurna"
  },
  "text": {
   "approach": "From Highway 97 south of the Y-junction, drive ~7.5 miles and turn onto Ingalls Creek Road/Trailhead. Hike the Ingalls Creek Trail roughly 8 miles, then leave the trail (right/north) into brushy terrain up Crystal Creek, gaining about 2,200 ft to a base-camp meadow and tarn near 6,000 ft. From the tarn, climb a large talus-apron gully west of the tarn to a col at roughly 7,700-7,880 ft between Little Annapurna and the spires to its south.",
   "approach_logistics": null,
   "road": "{\"name\":\"Ingalls Creek Road, off US-97 south of the US-2 junction\",\"status\":\"A short access road off the highway to a small trailhead lot at about 1,900 ft. A recreation pass is required to park, and a free wilderness permit is filled out at the trailhead.\",\"driveNote\":\"From the US-2/US-97 junction east of Leavenworth, follow US-97 south about seven miles, then turn west onto Ingalls Creek Road and continue roughly a mile to the trailhead. This is the Ingalls Creek side of the peak — a much longer walk in than the Enchantments approach, and a different drive entirely.\",\"seasonalGate\":\"No seaso",
   "overview": "A rarely-climbed, two-pitch 5.5-5.6 rock route straight up Little Annapurna's steep true south face, approached from the seldom-used Ingalls Creek/Crystal Creek side rather than the Enchantments basin.",
   "description": null,
   "descent": "From the summit plateau, descend north/northeast down talus and slab slopes toward Crystal Lake, then pick up the outlet stream drainage and follow it back down to the Crystal Creek base-camp meadow/tarn, retracing the approach back to Ingalls Creek Trail."
  },
